From: LLCOOLT <114613597+LLCOOLT@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:40:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gx: bounding box from the drawn vertices

GXClearBoundingBox writes BP 0x55/0x56, which arm a CPU bounding box; while
armed, each draw's positions (direct or indexed, any component type) are
transformed by their position matrix, the projection and the viewport.
GXReadBoundingBox processes the queued draws (GXDrawDone) and returns that
extent clamped to the scissor, or the hardware's empty box (left > right)
when nothing was drawn; a vertex that cannot be placed (behind the eye, an
unreadable array) reports the whole scissor. Games size offscreen captures
(paper-form models, shadows) and cull with it.
---
--- a/lib/dolphin/gx/GXFrameBuffer.cpp
+++ b/lib/dolphin/gx/GXFrameBuffer.cpp
@@ -248,6 +248,13 @@
 u16 GXGetNumXfbLines(u16 efbHeight, f32 yScale) {
   return get_num_xfb_lines(efbHeight, static_cast<u32>(256.0f / yScale) & 0x1FF);
 }
-// TODO GXClearBoundingBox
-// TODO GXReadBoundingBox
+void GXClearBoundingBox() {
+  GX_WRITE_RAS_REG(0x550003FF);
+  GX_WRITE_RAS_REG(0x560003FF);
 }
+
+void GXReadBoundingBox(u16* left, u16* top, u16* right, u16* bottom) {
+  GXDrawDone(); // the draws since the clear processed (aurora::gx::bbox_read)
+  aurora::gx::bbox_read(left, top, right, bottom);
+}
+}
--- a/lib/gx/command_processor.cpp
+++ b/lib/gx/command_processor.cpp
@@ -14,7 +14,9 @@
